  "previousRemaining": 636,
  "evidenceRule": "Each authored question must genuinely require its frozen target sentence. Preserve exact PDF-derived text.",
  "targets": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0078",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s05-p110-02625-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In the late 1940s, social psychologists Leon Festinger, Stan Schachter, and Kurt Back were also interested in distance and relationships when they set out to examine friendship formation in two MIT residential complexes: Westgate and Westgate West.",
      "sentenceSha256": "6b2e1793b9294daacf7f7f9c43299835f6ffcfd2a4ae901f75ad538dfa7f6a0a",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s05-p110-02625-r001-002",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-042",
      "parentFingerprint": "c61b507a1b115c78d1e53f9317918515e5eeefde0c8fb5db76eab832f2df06e7",
      "passageSha256": "132ebd5d6c8477f4d1a8a46c0bff9038ed23f8a35941f4b9491e1d80c0788e20",
      "pdfPages": [
        110
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0079",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s05-p110-03990-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Festinger and colleagues knew exactly where all the participants in this study lived, and asked one simple question: “What three people in Westgate or Westgate West do you see most of socially?”",
      "sentenceSha256": "4c1ef47d3508ebfe6176fb2440970983401c46e05758bd4fccffc4a383918fd9",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s05-p110-03990-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-043",
      "parentFingerprint": "764c51a47dcb0c3fa01d330335cf1b8c1c519d4486378e22409d70d980c68d1a",
      "passageSha256": "c81b7230e6bfccccf7775ea85f61c18957196ab699891264410b7bd915e2a440",
      "pdfPages": [
        110
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 3,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0080",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s05-p110-03990-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Only seven nominations were made of someone living four units away or more.",
      "sentenceSha256": "274180a20152698db02b5b4479f33173950cb486615f0a099b2092d43b68a04f",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s05-p110-03990-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-043",
      "parentFingerprint": "764c51a47dcb0c3fa01d330335cf1b8c1c519d4486378e22409d70d980c68d1a",
      "passageSha256": "c81b7230e6bfccccf7775ea85f61c18957196ab699891264410b7bd915e2a440",
      "pdfPages": [
        110
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 4,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0081",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s05-p110-03990-s004",
      "sentenceText": "So, physical distance clearly matters.",
      "sentenceSha256": "359813e634061a602296b31f4369dabb22f60a1de5b7effb4725fdb78662029c",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s05-p110-03990-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-043",
      "parentFingerprint": "764c51a47dcb0c3fa01d330335cf1b8c1c519d4486378e22409d70d980c68d1a",
      "passageSha256": "c81b7230e6bfccccf7775ea85f61c18957196ab699891264410b7bd915e2a440",
      "pdfPages": [
        110
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 5,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0082",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s05-p110-03990-s005",
      "sentenceText": "The other interesting finding from the study was that functional distance also matters.",
      "sentenceSha256": "9b77710a01648a229929b623676e5a55b46868fb6f856df9e79ee0c888bc530e",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s05-p110-03990-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-044",
      "parentFingerprint": "7ae17eba32ade46b8e9660a0a8be0268a89e364bde655c12686db864c84f8fe9",
      "passageSha256": "c749e902cd47424342a48146fe3c65fc2846a6d8ba49fe798243e3c234f916db",
      "pdfPages": [
        110
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 6,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0083",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-01650-s002",
      "sentenceText": "What repeated chance meetings do is increase familiarity.",
      "sentenceSha256": "2307bd462b63ae0ef922defd2aff0de9f2edc3bfb22d103cdf35885f93e83685",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-01650-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-046",
      "parentFingerprint": "5bf700c363ebc9e99ba6240987e26e72cc6f1f3f097f912799cb29c85c970bff",
      "passageSha256": "ef32578cf8c81d937e1dbc4b493e00594cd185906e1dd19a80053049bd820db4",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 7,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0084",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-01650-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Bob Zajonc, one of the greatest social psychologists of all time, zeroed in on the familiarity effect, or what he called the “mere exposure effect,” in a series of experiments.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7776e1fde7522d6736ad130793188bdb951e13530d98933d426b13626c0634e4",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-01650-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-046",
      "parentFingerprint": "5bf700c363ebc9e99ba6240987e26e72cc6f1f3f097f912799cb29c85c970bff",
      "passageSha256": "ef32578cf8c81d937e1dbc4b493e00594cd185906e1dd19a80053049bd820db4",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 8,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0085",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Even before he conducted this series of experiments, Zajonc made an ingenious refinement of previous research on word frequency and its link to perceived “desirability” of a word (i.e., how good or bad a word sounds).",
      "sentenceSha256": "b2325b45c13e35f9487eb61a0c259e4786a8293d20092e4b5038f893224025be",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-047",
      "parentFingerprint": "a013dfcb903378c967410977b6481caa4d7c44c047110ac9a91af8828a60b0fe",
      "passageSha256": "7f32036b91987a6b863219c2d80e5154615de7db133ae3d78f776acacd74a39b",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 9,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0086",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Word frequency was measured by how often each word appeared in published books and magazines in the 1920s and 1930s, in painstaking work conducted by Edward Thorndike and Irving Lorge.",
      "sentenceSha256": "0d9fb248435d56a3915cfb1994ffa1ea35eb7c3a5a463dd58d300561f0b29578",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-047",
      "parentFingerprint": "a013dfcb903378c967410977b6481caa4d7c44c047110ac9a91af8828a60b0fe",
      "passageSha256": "7f32036b91987a6b863219c2d80e5154615de7db133ae3d78f776acacd74a39b",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 10,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0087",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-s004",
      "sentenceText": "Everyone agrees that the word “good” is good, but not as good as the word “better.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "5bd6bac09cd44505826e441cec5ff14e82d6f7823d2c39b809398932d3319ae7",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-r004-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-048",
      "parentFingerprint": "0e6fe236fa4ade885a842384e76dba8f8b7b88f49e604bdcd127b154df57e81b",
      "passageSha256": "36386d6d92d6906fc088732da078c3b09f6e9fc5b6eccd50ef7a8e6fe6ed3f0c",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 11,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0088",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-s006",
      "sentenceText": "So, if frequent encounters increase the desirability of a word, then the word “good” should be more desirable than the word “better.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "1b1f95c0f69b9c5d49c6410273032540f8d7f73e4e619c58b081eb60798a410b",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-r004-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-048",
      "parentFingerprint": "0e6fe236fa4ade885a842384e76dba8f8b7b88f49e604bdcd127b154df57e81b",
      "passageSha256": "36386d6d92d6906fc088732da078c3b09f6e9fc5b6eccd50ef7a8e6fe6ed3f0c",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0089",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-s007",
      "sentenceText": "Indeed, participants in a psychology experiment reported that the word “good” is more desirable than the word “better”!",
      "sentenceSha256": "8ee7e4d1e1d7863d12788bfacf80415bce7ff38371f03420df2ec9c431d5c52d",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-02820-r004-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-048",
      "parentFingerprint": "0e6fe236fa4ade885a842384e76dba8f8b7b88f49e604bdcd127b154df57e81b",
      "passageSha256": "36386d6d92d6906fc088732da078c3b09f6e9fc5b6eccd50ef7a8e6fe6ed3f0c",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0090",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-s001",
      "sentenceText": "The findings from this research on word frequency are fascinating, but they are still correlational.",
      "sentenceSha256": "4c57af0db29b1239cac2c3358d8c92ed281254bbaa917d5bf3654ee918cb6808",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-049",
      "parentFingerprint": "aaa9624e718eddb207f7da7d53a6dc8425c3779307e62195660de8980b26b6de",
      "passageSha256": "c90eaac833dc011593254013cf0f5ce314eb0439ede73bbe4f6de48c346c0227",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0091",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-s003",
      "sentenceText": "So Zajonc designed an experiment in which participants were presented with nonsense words such as “iktitaf,” “afworbu,” and “saricik.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "4c7ec226815bfa77e272930b84b07e46e1cf6eba5523f5c6c119134734200c27",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-049",
      "parentFingerprint": "aaa9624e718eddb207f7da7d53a6dc8425c3779307e62195660de8980b26b6de",
      "passageSha256": "c90eaac833dc011593254013cf0f5ce314eb0439ede73bbe4f6de48c346c0227",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 15,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0092",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-s004",
      "sentenceText": "The experimenter told the participants that these were “Turkish” words (they weren’t) and showed them how to pronounce each.",
      "sentenceSha256": "a351cdc8311240125516dd3f07cce8e83ce32a802235126e450c06c1fd7af6cd",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-049",
      "parentFingerprint": "aaa9624e718eddb207f7da7d53a6dc8425c3779307e62195660de8980b26b6de",
      "passageSha256": "c90eaac833dc011593254013cf0f5ce314eb0439ede73bbe4f6de48c346c0227",
      "pdfPages": [
        111
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 16,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0093",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-s005",
      "sentenceText": "The participants were then asked to pronounce each word.",
      "sentenceSha256": "01bdf2c59ece7d48b8cee94d9e6764ee2619d38021ae853a666d7dec4b2984e7",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-050",
      "parentFingerprint": "4254396af19e3698b246ec755f517fb72ba3e8daae7c85797a579e7cb070ff9f",
      "passageSha256": "aff5ddcc439a0e83d392595aca0550069f79c407d208c5ca89726d3b4cece18d",
      "pdfPages": [
        111,
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 17,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0094",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-s006",
      "sentenceText": "Afterward, they were asked to guess the meaning of each “Turkish” word in terms of how good or bad they are.",
      "sentenceSha256": "49c40434796669b3829b1f391c3eecdd2728b82964b9c17a276d5700ddee0406",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-050",
      "parentFingerprint": "4254396af19e3698b246ec755f517fb72ba3e8daae7c85797a579e7cb070ff9f",
      "passageSha256": "aff5ddcc439a0e83d392595aca0550069f79c407d208c5ca89726d3b4cece18d",
      "pdfPages": [
        111,
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 18,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0095",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-s008",
      "sentenceText": "That was how Zajonc manipulated familiarity.",
      "sentenceSha256": "c07899ca07b9ab6cfb573cc8c721e7414b6a306a00a0e37ac531438228578334",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-050",
      "parentFingerprint": "4254396af19e3698b246ec755f517fb72ba3e8daae7c85797a579e7cb070ff9f",
      "passageSha256": "aff5ddcc439a0e83d392595aca0550069f79c407d208c5ca89726d3b4cece18d",
      "pdfPages": [
        111,
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 19,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0096",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-s010",
      "sentenceText": "He then replicated this initial finding with Chinese characters.",
      "sentenceSha256": "0150653a887d6aa6979f948687db158d2e13ee6a57d418a4c36c85b39af16290",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p111-05355-r009-011",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-051",
      "parentFingerprint": "4e941d878f1e6794de74ef2472ec90e9fad2978c00c85c21920b5b9a685be96a",
      "passageSha256": "eb1faf69fbdea83e55d4375f0df79068eab970c8fb15906705874d0d28bc4810",
      "pdfPages": [
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 20,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0097",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p112-02310-s001",
      "sentenceText": "The story of the mere exposure effect doesn’t stop here.",
      "sentenceSha256": "57b4380bcfb82ea2b9a6eb05fb7eb52bf5d675f778079eeab47624c9d26e0fea",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p112-02310-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-052",
      "parentFingerprint": "96b3c210d8ab5be9ba30226a899ea9cd73137f539e51d24b52a49fa37cf4c0e2",
      "passageSha256": "fef43039b1a38abf75a499687055b5600da28b0c0f1d43da1aad0c2e939f70f8",
      "pdfPages": [
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 21,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0098",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p112-02310-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Richard Moreland and Bob Zajonc ran a field experiment in a real college classroom.",
      "sentenceSha256": "13234f872db5040a75a68421a6b312ffe86281d90b7771b5cab22fe42e3f103e",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p112-02310-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-052",
      "parentFingerprint": "96b3c210d8ab5be9ba30226a899ea9cd73137f539e51d24b52a49fa37cf4c0e2",
      "passageSha256": "fef43039b1a38abf75a499687055b5600da28b0c0f1d43da1aad0c2e939f70f8",
      "pdfPages": [
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 22,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0099",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p112-02310-s006",
      "sentenceText": "They were all dressed in a casual fashion.",
      "sentenceSha256": "3a72094e098b0503c4f4a4a2aef29e722d71471681f266a00a1bec402155f641",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p112-02310-r005-006",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-053",
      "parentFingerprint": "58bbcf7fa2f29a25f0ade5bf1af2f2899892182efaa6953d96632b85b1d3b816",
      "passageSha256": "75920666c88c50088228c71936c162c780fdad65d25fde899cb1471ed2c0c618",
      "pdfPages": [
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 23,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0100",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p112-05625-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Likewise, more exposure was associated with more perceived similarities, as well.",
      "sentenceSha256": "a67fc2c0879e631946d7af3b26828681c86f19dc87943a7eda00591f9291a006",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p112-05625-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-056",
      "parentFingerprint": "1b5554725e024c246727c41cb31da5ef0fcd6aaaed4de553265f82ba2d55269d",
      "passageSha256": "1a15b6a0f39765273da7447ecfcd15575ceba3d26667f0d8ed1a1eedc4090cb9",
      "pdfPages": [
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 24,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0101",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p112-05625-s003",
      "sentenceText": "For instance, when students were explicitly asked whether they knew these four women, nobody said yes.",
      "sentenceSha256": "36e37698a64a64423103eb95755443163aa02644829337b714ea5edf121e7864",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p112-05625-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-056",
      "parentFingerprint": "1b5554725e024c246727c41cb31da5ef0fcd6aaaed4de553265f82ba2d55269d",
      "passageSha256": "1a15b6a0f39765273da7447ecfcd15575ceba3d26667f0d8ed1a1eedc4090cb9",
      "pdfPages": [
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 25,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0102",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s06-p113-00750-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Previous research already convincingly demonstrated that perceived similarity leads to attraction.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7cebb643ede164d3aaeba1649218b9d2277b8678466c5c6ccad575fdeb1413d7",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s06-p113-00750-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-058",
      "parentFingerprint": "3c3ede7f24bcdb6f1ad3ddc57562077379ee75a382aa712bfb6f4f3d6e4066dd",
      "passageSha256": "76fd9e1abb582cab6386a8af26f2ff50b923228f7fcff43832d0d22fd327cd83",
      "pdfPages": [
        113
      ]
    }
  ]
}
